pport Services\nIQAC\nNIRF\nCollege Journal\nSubmission Gateway\nRecord Keeping\nTeacher Publication\nTeacher Seminar/Conference\nTeacher Workshop/PDP/FDP/FIP/RC/OP/STTP/Webinar\nStudents' Corner\nAlumni Association\nCollege Rules & Regulations\nStudents' Union Body\nGrievance Submission Link\nSessional Marks Statement\nScholarship Details\nStudent Feedback Link\nLibrary Website\nGallery\nPhotos\nVideos\nAnti-Ragging\nFacebook\nTwitter\nYoutube\nCOMMERCE DEPARTMENT\nPrevious\nNext\nDepartment Notice |\nView All\nClass Test of B. Com 4th and 6th Semester\nClick Here\nMicrofinance[R]_6th Sem_Assignment_2024\nClick Here\nMicrofinance[H]_4th Sem_Assignment_2024\nClick Here\nAssignment_FOI_2024\nClick Here\nBanking [R] Assignment_2024\nClick Here\nHoliday List_2023\nClick Here\nViva_Notice_B. Com_5th_Semester_Banking_Subject\nClick Here\nViva_Notice_B.Com_5th_Semester_Banking_Subject\nClick Here\nViva_Notice_B.Com_1st_Semester\nClick Here\nB. Com 1st_Semester_Class_Test\nClick Here\nDepartment Profile\nThe Department of Commerce was established in the month of August 2017, with a vision of providing excellence in the fields of Commerce by imparting value-based education, training and research. Since its inception, the primary aim of the Department has been to make the student diagnose and respond to change in social realities through the development and application of knowledge. The aim of the department is to focus on a skill-based outreach Programme that would help the student to serve the society efficiently across the wide range of emerging humanitarian challenges in the globalized era. The department is making its utmost effort to make the Department the world class best place for Commerce education taking different layers of academics, research, outreach and extension activities.\nVision:\nFrom its inception, the Department is committed to integrate all facets of business and commerce to educate and train competent human resource globally suitable for industry, business and service sector; and to equip and encourage them to start their own ventures in urban or rural areas benefitting both the classes and masses.\nMission:\nWe are dedicated to secure and deliver knowledge through teaching, research and extension; and to seek continuous improvement in the quality of education to remain globally competitive.\nFaculty Members\nMAHESH DAHAL\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR\nmaheshdahal118@gmail.com\nView Profile\nROTNALI MAIBANGSA\nASSISTANT PROFESSOR, HOD\nmerlynmiss1@gmail.com\nView Profile\nEx- Faculty Members\nName\nDesignation\nDate of Joining\nDate of Retirement/Resign\nPhoto\nActivities\nID\nTitle\nDescription\nPublish\nView File\nAchievements\nID\nTitle\nDate\nView\nQuestion Paper\nID\nSemester\nyear\nView\n36\n2nd Semester\n2023\nView File\n37\n4th Semester\n2022\nView File\n39\n6th Semester\n2023\nView File\n38\n6th Semester\n2022\nView File\n40\n6th Semester\n2022\nView File\nSyllabus\nID\nTitle\nDate\nView\n30\nTDC_Commerce_ (Non-CBCS)\n2023-11-07\nView File\n29\nH.S. 1st_Year\n2023-11-07\nView File\n28\nTDC_Commerce_ (Non-CBCS)\n2023-11-07\nView File\n27\nB.Com_Reg_CBCS\n2023-11-07\nView File\n26\nB. Com_Hon_CBCS\n2023-11-07\nView File\nStudy Materials\nID\nTitle\nSemester\nView\n5\nIndian Banking System\n5th Semester\nView File\n4\nModern Banking System\n5th Semester\nView File\n3\nIndian Financial System_New\n1st Semester\nView File\n2\nIndian Financial System\n5th Semester\nView File\n1\nIndian Financial System\n1st Semester\nView File\nAdd-on/Certificate Courses\nID\nSl. No.\nCourse Type\nSession\nCourse Name\nStudents Enrolled\nCourse Completion\nView\n4\n1\nAdd-on\n2022-23\nFundamentals of Finance and Investment\n17\n16-05-2023\nView File\nMoU\nSl. No.\nMoU Parties\nTime Period\nView File\nContact Us\n&nbspPandit Deendayal Upadhyaya Adarsha Mahavidyalaya,\nTulungia\nP.O- North Salmara\nDist: Bongaigaon, Assam -783383\n&nbsppduamtulungia@gmail.com\n+91 8638105324\nVisitors Counter\nImportant Links\ngauhati university\nUGC\nA